{"question_text": {"স্পেশাল বিসিএস (স্বাস্থ্য) - লং কোর্স": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Calculation of the BODE index exclude ", "option1": "FEV1", "option2": "Distance walked in 6 hour(m)", "option3": "mMRC dyspnoea scale", "option4": "Body mass index", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_211607_wN0RUVw.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"419\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Gene of CFTR is situated in chromosome", "option1": "7", "option2": "8", "option3": "9", "option4": "6", "answer": "1", "exp": "<span style=\"color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px; background-color: #f2f2f2;\">CF is the result of pathogenic variants affecting a gene on&nbsp;</span><u style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px; background-color: #f2f2f2;\"><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bolder;\">the long&nbsp;arm of chromosome 7,</span></u><span style=\"color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px; background-color: #f2f2f2;\">&nbsp;which codes for a chloride channel known as cystic brosis transmembrane conductance regulator (CFTR); this infuences salt and water movement across epithelial cell membranes.</span>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Time frame of HAP is  at least ----------- hour after admission", "option1": "24 hour", "option2": "36 hour", "option3": "48 hour", "option4": "72 hour", "answer": "3", "exp": "<br />\r\n<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\"><u style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bolder;\">Hospital-acquired pneumonia</span></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\">Hospital-acquired pneumonia (HAP) is defined as an episode of pneumonia&nbsp;that presents<span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bolder;\">&nbsp;at least 48 hours after admission to hospital</span>&nbsp;and was not incubating at the time of admission. It is the second most common healthcare-associated infection (HAI) after surgical-site infections and the leading cause of HAI-associated death. Older patients are particularly at risk, as are patients in intensive care units. The term ventilator-associated pneumonia (VAP) is used to describe pneumonia that develops in a person who is mechanically ventilated.</div>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Poor  dental hygiene is associated with ", "option1": "Actinomyces", "option2": "Stap. aureaus", "option3": "Stap. Epidermidis", "option4": "Nocardia", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\">Infections are usually due to a mixture of anaerobes and aerobes in common with the typical flora encountered in the mouth and upper respiratory tract. Isolates of Prevotella melaninogenica, Fusobacterium necrophorum,&nbsp;anaerobic or microaerophilic cocci and Bacteroides fragili may be identified. When suppurative pneumonia or a pulmonary abscess</div>\r\n<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\">occurs in a previously healthy lung, the most likely infecting organisms&nbsp;&nbsp;are Staph. aureus or K. pneumoniae.<u style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bolder;\">&nbsp;Actinomyces spp. cause chronic suppurative pulmonary infections, which may be associated with poor dental hygiene.</span></u></div>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) First-choice oral antibiotic for non-severe symptoms or signs and not at higher risk of resistance", "option1": "Co-amoxiclav", "option2": "Meropenem", "option3": "Co-trimoxazole", "option4": "Vancomycin", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_213130_yTrbb11_MK7eVHz.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"409\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) ß-1,3-D-glucan levels are characteristically elevated in", "option1": "P. jirovecii pneumonia", "option2": "Strep Pneumonia", "option3": "Virus", "option4": "Legionella ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<u style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bolder;\">&szlig;-1,3-D-glucan levels are characteristically elevated in P. jirovecii&nbsp;pneumonia.</span></u><br style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\" />\r\n<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\">Focal unilateral airspace opacication favours bacterial infection,mycobacteria or Nocardia.</div>\r\n<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\">Bilateral opacication favours P. jirovecii pneumonia, fungi, viruses and unusual bacteria, e.g. Nocardia</div>\r\n<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\">cavitation may be seen with N. asteroides, mycobacteria and fungi&nbsp;&nbsp;the presence of a &lsquo;halo sign&rsquo; (a zone of intermediate attenuation between the nodule and the lung parenchyma) may suggest aspergillosis or other invasive fungal infection&nbsp; pleural effusions suggest pyogenic bacterial infections and are uncommon in P. jirovecii pneumonia.</div>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Bone marrow finding of miliary TB", "option1": "Leukopenia", "option2": "Leukocytosis", "option3": "Neutrophilia", "option4": "Thrombocytopenia", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\">Miliary TB</div>\r\n<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\">Blood-borne dissemination gives rise to miliary TB, which may present&nbsp;acutely but more frequently is characterised by 2&ndash;3 weeks of fever, night&nbsp;sweats, anorexia, weight loss and a dry cough. Hepatosplenomegaly&nbsp;may develop and the presence of a headache may indicate coexistent&nbsp;tuberculous meningitis. Auscultation of the chest is frequently normal but</div>\r\n<div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px;\">in more advanced disease widespread crackles are evident. Fundoscopy&nbsp;may show choroidal tubercles. The classical appearances on chest X-ray&nbsp;are of ne 1&ndash;2 mm lesions (&lsquo;millet seed&rsquo;) distributed throughout the lung&nbsp;elds, although occasionally the appearances are coarser.&nbsp;<u style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bolder;\">Anaemia and leucopenia refect bone marrow involvement</span></u></div>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Which is not a hypersrnsitivity reaction in Primary TB", "option1": "Phlyctenular conjunctivitis", "option2": "Erythema nodosum", "option3": "Dactylitis", "option4": "Obstructive emphysema", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_215013_zOm5Q3g.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"506\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Hemolytic anemia is a side effect of ", "option1": "Rifampicin", "option2": "INH", "option3": "Ethambutol", "option4": "Streptomycin", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_220101.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"196\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Tuberculin skin test is positive when induration is greater than", "option1": "5cm", "option2": "5mm", "option3": "5inch", "option4": "0.5 mm", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_220314.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"117\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which is not a features of  of allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis", "option1": "Elevated total serum IgE >417 kU/L", "option2": "Recovery of A. fumigatus from sputum", "option3": "COPD", "option4": "Proximal bronchiectasis (inner two-thirds of chest CT eld)", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_221220.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"334\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Less commonn cause of lung  cancer", "option1": "Adenocarcinoma", "option2": "Large-cell", "option3": "Squamous", "option4": "Small-cell", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_221727.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"272\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Survival rate of carcinoid tumor is", "option1": "95%", "option2": "85%", "option3": "75%", "option4": "65%", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_221943.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"244\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Feature of SVCO obstruction", "option1": "pulsatile distension of neck veins", "option2": "conjunctival oedema", "option3": "dilated anastomotic veins on chest wall", "option4": " acyanosis of head, neck, hands and arms", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_222319.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"113\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) HRCT finding of DPLD", "option1": "ground glass changes", "option2": "reticulonodular shadowing", "option3": "honeycomb cysts", "option4": "ALL", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_222409.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"534\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Which of the following ion is associated with Investigations in diffuse parenchymal lung disease", "option1": "Ca", "option2": "K", "option3": "Na", "option4": "Cl", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_222721.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"315\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) There are __________ stages in CXR of a sarcoidoisis Patient", "option1": "3", "option2": "4", "option3": "5", "option4": "6", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_222835.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"426\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Most Common Pulmonary feat in RA?", "option1": "Fibrosis", "option2": "Respiratory failure", "option3": "Sarcoisoisis", "option4": "Lung cancer", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_223102_N0LjmT0.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"414\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Lung cancer is found in ", "option1": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "option2": "Systemic lupus erythematosus", "option3": "Granulomatosis with polyangiitis (GPA)", "option4": "Dermatomyositis/\r\npolymyositis", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_223320.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"238\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Hidebound chest is found in ", "option1": "SS", "option2": "SLE", "option3": "RA", "option4": "DM", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_223510.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"271\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Acute eosinophilic pneumonia is an acute febrile illness (of less than_____________days characterised by diffuse pulmonary infiltrates and\r\nhypoxic respiratory failure", "option1": "3", "option2": "4", "option3": "5", "option4": "6", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div>Acute eosinophilic pneumonia is an acute febrile illness (of less than&nbsp;5 days&rsquo; duration), characterised by diffuse pulmonary infilltrates and hypoxic respiratory failure.</div>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Drug cause of Pulmonary eosinophila", "option1": "para-aminosalicylic acid (PAS", "option2": "sulfasalazine", "option3": "nitrofurantoin", "option4": "All", "answer": "4", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_223945.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"226\" />,&nbsp;</div>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Non-eosinophilic alveolitis is caused by ", "option1": "methotrexate", "option2": "gold", "option3": "mitomycin C", "option4": "All", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_224204.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"280\" />"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Caplan syndrome is a syndrome of ----------------------diameter rounded nodule", "option1": "0.5 cm", "option2": "0.5mm", "option3": "5mm", "option4": "0.5m", "answer": "1", "exp": "<span style=\"color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px; background-color: #f2f2f2;\">Caplan syndrome describes the coexistence of rheumatoid arthritis&nbsp;and rounded&nbsp;</span><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bolder; color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px; background-color: #f2f2f2;\">fibrotic nodules 0.5&ndash;5 cm in diameter</span><span style=\"color: #212529; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Noto Sans', 'Liberation Sans', Arial, sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji'; font-size: 16px; background-color: #f2f2f2;\">. They show pathological features similar to a rheumatoid nodule, including central necrosis, palisading histiocytes, and a peripheral rim of lymphocytes and plasma cells. This syndrome may also occur in other types of pneumoconiosis</span>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Arc welding is associated with ", "option1": "Coal dust", "option2": "Beryllium", "option3": "Iron oxide", "option4": "Tin Oxide", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_230700_xTqf2PW_TqAPGA2.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"455\" />"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Exposure to beryllium is encountered in ", "option1": "the aerospace", "option2": "engineering", "option3": "telecommunications", "option4": "ALL", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_231020_canILLD.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"415\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Maple bark stripper’s  lung is found i n ", "option1": "Aspergillus fumigatus", "option2": "Saccharopolyspora", "option3": "Cryptostroma corticale", "option4": "Cotton", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_231314_oU4i9KN.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"595\" />"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Predictive factors in the identification of hypersensitivity pneumonitis", "option1": "Expiratory crackles on examination", "option2": "Symptoms occurring 4–8 days after exposure", "option3": "Weight gain", "option4": " Inspiratory crackles on examination", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_231434_C8BKtOJ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"239\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) (wool-sorter’s disease) is", "option1": "Anthrax", "option2": "Diptheria", "option3": "TB", "option4": "Tetanus", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_231948_3C66qNk.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"577\" />"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Which is not a feature of Acute massive PE?", "option1": " hypotension", "option2": "↑JVP", "option3": "RV gallop rhythm", "option4": "loud P1", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_232256_Qk1qBFI.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"313\" />"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) CTPA is the first-line diagnostic test in", "option1": "PE", "option2": "RA", "option3": "BA", "option4": "SLE", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-02_232424_RKhywRf.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"138\" />"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Dose of Oral Prednisolone in COPD is", "option1": "10", "option2": "20", "option3": "30", "option4": "40", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-03_120630.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"178\" />"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Walks slower than contemporaries on level ground -grade it on MRC scale", "option1": "2", "option2": "3", "option3": "4", "option4": "5", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-03_130714.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"519\" />"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) occupational irritant for COPD is", "option1": "coal dus", "option2": " silica", "option3": "cadmium", "option4": "All", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-03_131008.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"426\" />"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) Regular preventer for Asthma", "option1": "Low dose ICS", "option2": "LTRA", "option3": "inhaled LABA", "option4": "Short-acting B2 agonists", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2024-05-03_131551.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"332\" />"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) Which of